2026-09-02T08:52:00.000Z note (out-of-band: GO-5 discharged, and the merged requirement's attribution for it is corrected here because only the operator can correct it. §1 and RK-2 call packages/shared/test/corpus.js and corpus.d.ts "tsc output from run 1", which reads as the engine having emitted them. It did not. They are MINE: a hand probe run at 07:14 UTC — during run 1's pm-claude step — testing whether `tsc -p packages/shared/tsconfig.json` could emit, which failed TS6059 because src/*.test.ts imports ../test/corpus.js from outside rootDir, and TypeScript then fell back to the common source directory and wrote the two files beside their source instead of into the --outDir I gave it. So the finding is right in every particular except who did it, and the harness engine emits no stray files. Both removed; `pnpm --filter @quorum/shared lint` green afterwards and `git status` clean but for this ticket's own artifacts. Recorded rather than quietly cleaned because they were present for the whole of run 1 and run 2 and were therefore visible to four candidate steps — the run-2 claude candidate found them and the merged requirement raised them as RK-2 and GO-5, which is the requirement catching the operator, and worth keeping for that reason alone. No test verdict was affected: the requirements flow runs no suite, so nothing executed while they were on disk, and they were untracked-unignored rather than tracked.)
